ts operative section says staff may not use a name or pronouns that don't match biological sex \"without written authorization from the pupil’s parent or legal guardian.\" That matches every clause of rung 5, so I coded it `chair-shaped`. Wittke wasn't a sponsor of this bill.\n- **AB 510 (2023, which he wrote) and AB 963 (2021, which he co-sponsored and voted for):** I coded both `direction-only`. Each gives parents a right to \"determine the names and pronouns used for the child while at school,\" but that right is one item in a long list. Neither bill says staff need permission first, so they show which side he is on but don't pick a rung.\n\nAll the passages are Assembly records, so I coded them `in-term`. His current term start is unknown, though, so code still has to confirm that each of these sessions falls within his service on file. There are no quotes, because none of the sources contain his own words, and `needs_source` is empty.","ttft_ms":21598,"type":"result","duration_ms":47792,"uuid":"d0f20d41-c9a0-4388-af65-934200a2417a","ttft_stream_ms":7006,"time_to_request_ms":232,"first_content_frame_ms":7006,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
